==English==
{{was wotd|2025|May|6}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|né}}{{root|en|ine-pro|*per-|id=fare|*(s)twerH-}}
From Late {{inh|en|enm|imperturbable|t=undisturbed; impossible to disturb}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=imperturbāble|pos=adj|id=MED22181}}</ref> borrowed from {{der|en|LL.|imperturbābilis}}, from {{der|en|la|im-}} (variant of {{m|la|in-|pos={{glossary|prefix}} meaning ‘not’}}) + {{der|en|LL.|perturbabilis|t=perturbable}}<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=adj|id=9122822325|date=September 2024|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=adj}}</ref> (from {{der|en|la|perturbō|t=to confuse; to alarm, disturb, trouble, perturb}} + {{m|la|-bilis|pos={{glossary|suffix}} forming {{glossary|adjective}}s denoting a capacity or worth of being acted upon}}). {{m|la||Perturbō}} is derived from {{m|la|per-|pos=prefix meaning ‘by means of; through’}} + {{m|la|turbō|t=to agitate, disturb, unsettle, perturb; to upset}} (from {{m|la|turba|t=disorder, disturbance, turmoil}} (possibly from {{der|en|grc|τῠ́ρβη|t=confusion, disorder, tumult}}, either from {{der|en|qsb-grc}}, or {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)twerH-|t=to agitate, stir up; to urge on, propel}}) + {{m|la|-ō|pos=suffix forming {{glossary|infinitive}}s of regular first-{{glossary|conjugation}} {{glossary|verb}}s}}. {{surf|en|im-|pos1=prefix meaning ‘not’|perturbable}}.

